meta {
  name: Refresh Token
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "refresh_token": "{{refresh_token}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  if (body && body.access_token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("jwt_token", body.access_token);
    bru.setEnvVar("refresh_token", body.refresh_token);
  }
}

docs {
  Rotate the access+refresh pair. Use when access_token has expired (or
  proactively before it does).

  Behavior:
    - Validates the refresh token (HS256, typ=refresh, exp, signature).
    - Confirms its jti is still in `sessions` (not revoked).
    - **Wipes ALL sessions for the device** before issuing the new pair.
      This is intentional: any previously-issued access tokens AND the old
      refresh token immediately stop working. If a stolen refresh token is
      used in parallel with the legitimate one, both clients get logged out
      and the device must re-authenticate via /auth/login.

  Failures:
    401 INVALID_TOKEN     → refresh signature/exp/typ failed, or revoked
    401 DEVICE_NOT_FOUND  → device deleted while session was alive
    401 DEVICE_INACTIVE   → device disabled
    429                   → rate limit

  On success the new access_token + refresh_token are written back into the
  Bruno env, replacing the previous values.
}
